# Sensor output: coverage, the mutation report, and Stryker's sandbox.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash, and that is load-bearing rather than tidiness.
# An unanchored pattern matches a directory of that name at any depth, so a bare
# `reports` also matched apps/web/src/features/reports — and Tailwind's source
# scanner honours .gitignore, so the whole Reports feature was invisible to it and
# `text-right`, `tabular-nums` and `xl:grid-cols-4` produced no CSS at all. The
# bare pattern arrived in eb514d4, the commit that added the sensor layer, and
# none of the five sensors in it could see what it broke. `npm run lint:classes`
# is what sees it now.
#
# All three are written at the repository root: stryker.config.json sets
# `htmlReporter.fileName` to reports/mutation/index.html and `tempDirName` to
# .stryker-tmp, and Vitest writes coverage beside the config it ran from.
/coverage
/reports
/.stryker-tmp
# Stryker's Vitest runner writes its sandbox setup file to the repository root
# rather than under tempDirName — one per worker, so eight on this machine. It is
# a known upstream limitation (stryker-js issue 5305); the file's own comment says
# it is copied into the sandbox and must not import anything local.
/stryker-setup-*.js

